9	//! # michi-core
10	//!
11	//! AXI response primitives for agent-ergonomic tools: TOON lists, key-value blocks, hints, structured errors, the
12	//! `AgentResponse` builder, truncation and retry policy. Async pipeline execution lives in
13	//! [`michi-pipeline`](https://docs.rs/michi-pipeline).
14	//!
15	//! michi turns structured data into token-efficient text an agent can read. Every agent-facing block (lists,
16	//! key-value items, errors, status, recovery hints) is a [TOON](https://github.com/toon-format/spec) document, so an
17	//! agent parses one format. The default build is synchronous and has no runtime dependencies beyond `thiserror` and
18	//! `compact_str`.
19	//!
20	//! ## Quick start
21	//!
22	//! ```
23	//! use michi_core::toon::{render_toon, ToonOptions, Value};
24	//!
25	//! let opts = ToonOptions::new(
26	//!     "issues",
27	//!     vec!["number".to_string(), "title".to_string(), "state".to_string()],
28	//!     vec![
29	//!         vec![Value::Int(51815), Value::from("[Bug]: Telegram plugin"), Value::from("open")],
30	//!         vec![Value::Int(51812), Value::from("dark mode request"), Value::from("open")],
31	//!     ],
32	//! )
33	//! .total_count(Some(8771));
34	//!
35	//! assert_eq!(
36	//!     render_toon(&opts)?,
37	//!     "issues[2]{number,title,state}:\n  51815,\"[Bug]: Telegram plugin\",open\n  51812,dark mode request,open\n\
38	//!      totalCount: 8771"
39	//! );
40	//! # Ok::<(), michi_core::toon::ToonError>(())
41	//! ```
42	//!
43	//! ## Where to start
44	//!
45	//! - [`toon`]: lists of rows, and `toon::list()` for `Serialize` types (`serde` feature).
46	//! - [`kv`]: one item as `key: value` lines.
47	//! - [`error`]: [`DomainError`] with a stable [`ErrorCode`] and agent-readable rendering.
48	//! - [`response`]: [`AgentResponse`], which composes the primitives into one reply.
49	//! - [`mcp`]: MCP `CallToolResult` assembly.
50	//! - [`resilience`]: retry delays, `Retry-After` parsing, retry budgets and idempotency keys.
51	//! - [`truncate`](mod@truncate): UTF-8 safe truncation of one string, with the cut reported outside the text.
52	//! - [`truncation`]: what a cap on a list cut ([`TruncationOutcome`]), however the survivors were chosen.
53	//!
54	//! ## Features
55	//!
56	//! | Feature | Adds |
57	//! | --- | --- |
58	//! | `serde` | `Serialize`/`Deserialize` on the data types, and `toon::list()` |
59	//! | `schemars` | `JsonSchema` on the DTO types, for MCP `outputSchema` (implies `serde`) |
60	//! | `miette` | `miette::Diagnostic` for [`DomainError`] |
61	//! | `napi` | The Node.js export surface used by `@orin-dx/michi` (needs a Node toolchain) |
62	//!
63	//! No features are on by default.
